{
   ── Managed Method ──
   Hook           : << HookNameParsed >>
   Process        : << Process >>
   Image          : << default(MonoImage, "unknown") >>
   Namespace      : << default(MonoNamespace, "(global namespace)") >>
   Class          : << MonoClass >>
   Method         : << MonoMethod >>
   Descriptor     : << MonoDescriptor >>

   ── Script Details ──
   Cheat Name     : << HookName >>
   Author         : Leunsel
   Date           : << Date >>
   Version        : << Version >>
   Method Entry   : resolved at assemble time
   Method Size    : $<< hex(MonoMethodSize) >>
   Injection      : entry +$<< hex(MonoMethodOffset) >>

   There is no signature here and no copy of the original bytes, which is
   deliberate. The method is JIT compiled, so its code is built fresh every
   time the process starts. A signature over it stops matching after a
   restart, and bytes written down now would be the wrong ones to put back
   later. The anchor is the name, FINDMONOMETHOD resolves it inside the
   target while the script assembles, and readMem takes the backup from
   whatever is really there at that moment.

